  "interpretation": [
    "Paired calibrated-minus-raw Brier intervals were below zero for every seed/model/horizon run, so recalibration consistently improved Brier score relative to raw class-weighted probabilities.",
    "Many Brier-minus-prevalence-reference intervals crossed zero, especially at 3 and 6 hours; the point estimates alone do not establish a reliable improvement over a prevalence-only reference.",
    "The prevalence reference uses the evaluated cohort's observed prevalence and is descriptive, not a deployable baseline trained independently of the test data.",
    "Intervals quantify patient-sampling uncertainty conditional on the fixed Set B cohort and fitted models; they do not establish prospective validity, clinical utility, or safety."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The Challenge label already incorporates a six-hour lead convention; targets predict entry into the Challenge-positive label window, not independently observed biological onset.",
    "Set B is a second Challenge training cohort, not prospective external clinical validation.",
    "Alerts outside future-positive windows are not verified clinical false alarms.",
    "VITALIS remains research-only and is not clinically validated."
  ],
